cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Please cite the preprint and its replay supplement. The manuscript text is licensed under CC-BY-4.0; the replay scripts and the remaining files are licensed under Apache-2.0.
title: 'Replay supplement for Obstructions to lifting cold-phonon pairing bounds to the full Gibbs state in the Holstein model'
authors:
- family-names: Rens
  given-names: Davis
  affiliation: SuperMatics Inc.
  orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5839-5197'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24419889
url: https://supermatics.io/research/full-gibbs-pairing-obstructions
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  The tagged release tree of the preprint "Obstructions to lifting cold-phonon pairing
  bounds to the full Gibbs state in the Holstein model": the reviewed manuscript source,
  the released PDF and six standalone replay scripts that check every finite arithmetic
  witness in exact rational and outward-interval arithmetic, with guarded mutant suites.
  The paper records why five natural route families fail to lift a released cold-projected
  pairing ceiling to the Gibbs state of the unprojected Holstein Hamiltonian at large U/Omega,
  quantifies a sixth route in the distortion coordinate, proves the hot-sector population
  bound with constant 1/4096 on the dimer and with volume-uniform constants on tori and
  finite vertex-transitive regular graphs, and isolates the remaining open statement. No
  pairing ceiling and no bound on any critical temperature is proved or disproved.
